As it stands now, all of the weapons are charged by reading a scroll
of enchant weapon, and that's it.  I would like some novel weapons
that have different ways of enchanting them.  For example ...

How about a stein?  It can be dropped by leprechauns (much like
unihorns are dropped by unicorns).  It's a one-handed weapon.  When
you #dip it into an uncursed potion of booze, it gets +1.  A blessed
potion of booze, +1 or +2.  A cursed potion of booze, -1.  This might
make booze actually have some uses :-)

In addition, you can burn off the stein's enchantments by (a)pplying
it to light it on fire.  This will reduce its enchantment to +0
(unless it was negative), and give it a fire bonus on its attack for
something like 500*(its level of pre-burn enchantment) turns.

The stein itself won't be a very good weapon (maybe just something
like 1d4 or 1d6), but it's useful because it gives you a good way to
use potions of booze, and when you (a)pply it and burn off those
potions, it actually becomes a formidable weapon (something along the
lines of Firebrand?).

So, what do you guys think?  Is it worth coding?

